coalesced interrupts: one byte, one wake
interrupts racing a park: no lost wake in every round
read readiness: notified once, removed on completion
write readiness: waits while full, notified when writable
registrations: removed on completion and cancellation, stale handles rejected
close during a poll: woken, registrations notified, pipe released
close on the owner and on drop: released once, registrations notified
close racing interrupts: released exactly once after every user left
timeouts: honored, including sub-millisecond deadlines
idle poll: no CPU over 500 ms
